86045585 true] [17592186399437 1071 "![](images/a7/a740aafbb9f74e2681506d3027f848fa92e7eea2bac3e08ccaf3fc7e0acf8fa1.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown in the graph above?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1072 #uuid "5cb8229e-2a6a-582b-a6c3-627b88cf6816" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399437 1074 "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399439 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399440 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399441 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399442 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399443 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399441 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399438 1080 #uuid "210acf01-110f-53da-bf3c-8725abe1a7d8" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399439 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399439 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 tru