533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399600 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399600 1084 #uuid "4f5b4306-4e52-5f8f-a6c5-d9a8c474f65b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399601 1081 "(7,-4,1)" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399601 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399601 1084 #uuid "b73612ac-9159-5b03-82b8-04dc3dbeb325" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399602 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399603 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399602 1069 "q-33205" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399602 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399602 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,-2,6⟩+t⟨2,5,4⟩,\\,Π:x+2y+z-33=0.\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399602 1072 #uuid "eaab1f60-24fb-5572-8cfb-474f418bf09f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399602 1074 "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z-33 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z & =33 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ ⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ -1+2t+2(-2+5t)+6+4t & =33 \\\\ -1+2t-4+10t+6+4t & =33 \\\\ 16t & =32 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+2(2),-2+5(2),6+4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,8,14⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(3,8,14).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399603 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399604 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399603 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399605 1