 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1071 "Consider a function $f(t)$ for which the Laplace transform is $L{f(t)}=F(s).$ How can we obtain the graph of $L{{e}^{-9t}f(t)}$ from the graph of $F(s)?$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1072 #uuid "f8dd5186-15e7-5cde-a17c-1b124d1cef2b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399609 1074 "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L{f(t)}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L{{e}^{-9t}f(t)},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $9$ units to the left." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399611 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399612 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399613 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399614 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399615 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399613 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399610 1080 #uuid "8decbbab-7268-5304-9585-788574a6793b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1081 "Scale the graph of $F(s)$ by a scale factor of $9$ horizontally." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399611 1084 #uuid "dbeddd1b-c3dd-54cd-a00c-bfa7f8bb9029" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 10